package com.bqsqwad.heartbreakhealer.feature.entertainment

/** Original ten-part story: The Courtyard of Many Languages. */
internal object StoryLibraryBatch53 {
    val stories = listOf(
        StorySeries(
            id = "the_courtyard_of_many_languages",
            title = "The Courtyard of Many Languages",
            tagline = "Students turn a neglected school courtyard into a welcoming place for language exchange.",
            parts = listOf(
                StoryPart(1, "A Quiet Corner", listOf(
                    "The courtyard behind the language block had become a storage area for broken chairs and unused noticeboards. When the school's language club asked for a place to hold conversation practice, teacher Mr Adeola suggested they first find out why the courtyard had been abandoned. A faded sign showed that it had once hosted an annual language festival.",
                    "Mina and her teammate Kalu photographed the public space from the path and made a list of what needed attention. They did not move the stored furniture or enter the locked shed. The caretaker explained that the courtyard had been closed after drainage problems and that the school needed to inspect it before students could use it again."
                )),
                StoryPart(2, "The Festival Programme", listOf(
                    "The school archive held programmes from three earlier language festivals. Each year, students had shared greetings, songs they had written themselves, short plays, and stories from family traditions. The programmes listed languages spoken by volunteers but did not record private family information. Mina thought the courtyard might be useful again if the school made the activities voluntary.",
                    "The club asked the head teacher for permission to propose a small pilot. The head teacher agreed to review a plan after the maintenance team assessed the drainage and seating. Mr Adeola reminded the students that nobody should be asked to represent an entire culture or speak a language they did not want to share."
                )),
                StoryPart(3, "The Drainage Report", listOf(
                    "The maintenance team inspected the courtyard and found that a blocked drain had caused water to collect near the shed. Staff cleared it and scheduled a follow-up check. They also identified two chairs that needed repair and recommended replacing a damaged noticeboard. Students were asked to keep clear of the work area until staff confirmed it was ready.",
                    "Mina updated the club plan with the maintenance team's notes. Kalu suggested movable seating so the space could be rearranged for different activities. The teacher liked the idea but asked them to include a clear route to the exit and keep the doorway unobstructed. The courtyard would need to work for everyone, not just the people presenting."
                )),
                StoryPart(4, "Invitations Without Pressure", listOf(
                    "The club drafted an invitation explaining that students could join as listeners, presenters, helpers, or audience members. Nobody had to share a personal story or explain their background. The invitation asked volunteers to offer a greeting, teach a useful phrase, or help make a multilingual sign if they wished.",
                    "A student suggested that every participant should wear traditional clothing. Mina disagreed because it could make people feel pressured to perform an identity. The club removed that suggestion and focused on language activities anyone could choose. Mr Adeola reviewed the invitation for respectful wording before it was posted."
                )),
                StoryPart(5, "The First Meeting", listOf(
                    "Students from several year groups attended the first planning meeting. Some wanted conversation tables, others preferred games or short performances. A few said they would rather help with posters than speak in front of a crowd. The club divided the work into small roles and let each volunteer choose what felt comfortable.",
                    "They agreed on a pilot afternoon with short sessions and quiet space for people who wanted to listen. A staff member would supervise, and the school would check any music or performance material before the event. Mina wrote down each decision so the next meeting would begin with a clear plan."
                )),
                StoryPart(6, "A Sign That Welcomes", listOf(
                    "The art club designed a sign with the words WELCOME in several languages chosen by volunteers. Each contributor checked the spelling and pronunciation of the phrase they supplied. The sign included a note that translations could vary by region and that visitors were welcome to suggest corrections politely.",
                    "The school print room produced a large, high-contrast version. The club placed it beside the courtyard entrance after the maintenance team confirmed the area was ready. A smaller notice explained the event schedule and reminded visitors that joining an activity was optional."
                )),
                StoryPart(7, "The Rainy Rehearsal", listOf(
                    "Rain interrupted the first rehearsal, and the club moved indoors according to its backup plan. The students tested the order of activities and discovered that one conversation table needed more time. Another activity depended on a speaker who could no longer attend. Instead of cancelling the whole session, the team adjusted the schedule and prepared a simple word game.",
                    "Mr Adeola praised the students for planning an alternative venue. They checked that the indoor room had enough space and that the route remained accessible. Mina added the revised plan to the shared folder so every volunteer would have the same information."
                )),
                StoryPart(8, "Festival Afternoon", listOf(
                    "The courtyard opened for the pilot festival on a bright afternoon. Visitors could join a greeting table, try a word puzzle, listen to short student-written stories, or simply sit and observe. Volunteers introduced each activity without asking anyone to explain where they came from. The staff adviser stayed nearby to help with questions.",
                    "A younger student taught Mina a greeting she had not heard before. Another visitor corrected a spelling on the sign kindly, and the club checked it with the contributor before making an update. The atmosphere was relaxed because the event offered many ways to participate."
                )),
                StoryPart(9, "What the Feedback Said", listOf(
                    "The club collected anonymous feedback cards. Visitors asked for more time at the conversation tables and suggested adding a quiet reading corner. One person said the instructions could be clearer for beginners. The students grouped the comments and discussed which changes were practical for the next event.",
                    "The head teacher approved a monthly session if the club maintained its supervision plan and checked the courtyard after each use. The maintenance team would continue its inspections. Mina realised that a welcoming place was not created by a sign alone; it needed listening, clear arrangements, and regular care."
                )),
                StoryPart(10, "A Courtyard Reopened", listOf(
                    "By the end of term, the courtyard had a simple schedule, movable seating, and a noticeboard for upcoming language activities. The school kept the original festival programmes in the archive and added the new event records. Volunteers could join without committing to every session, and the club welcomed listeners as much as presenters.",
                    "Mina stood by the multilingual sign and watched students choose their own ways to take part. The courtyard had not become a stage where everyone had to perform. It had become a shared place where people could learn from one another at their own pace. The quiet corner had found its voice by making room for many voices."
                ))
            )
        )
    )
}
